,\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He's / She's / It's\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We've\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You've\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "S + consonant sound combinations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Blends are combinations of two or three consonants that are voiced.</br> The following are examples: </br>Fl, bl, sl, cl, pl, bl, gr, tr, br, cr, dr, pr, fr, wh, str, sw, sp, sc, sn, sm, sk", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here are some examples of words with the sc consonant blend.</p> scared, score, scarf, screw", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Please pass me my scarf.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you scared of horror films?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chilly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "noticeably cold", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's been chilly in the evenings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation between two people.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to blush", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become red in your face because you are ashamed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now you are making me blush!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "like a school girl", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to behave in a childish way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Stop acting like a school girl.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to score", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get points, goals, or runs in a game or contest", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Maple Leafs just scored in the hockey game.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "abhorrent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing or deserving strong dislike or hatred", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have a reservation and the traffic is abhorrent this time of night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le12ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Interview your partner. Ask five questions. Find out what sporting activities they have done and haven't done in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use three words with the consonant blend sc like <span class=\"italic\">scared</span>, <span class=\"italic\">scored</span>, <span class=\"italic\">school</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down your partner's answers in complete sentences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I interview a partner about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use words with the consonant blend sc in a sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my dialogue about what I have done to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}